# The affiant-protocol ref this repository's conformance driver is pinned to.
#
# Versions of the rulebook (https://github.com/Sakwala/affiant-protocol) are git tags.
# The pin is the v0.2.0 tag, and `commit` records what that tag points at, so a reader
# can check one against the other with no network. While a version's text is on the
# rulebook's default branch and its tag has not been cut, `tag` is empty and the COMMIT
# is the pin: a commit is as immutable as a tag and, unlike a tag, cannot be moved
# under a running build.
#
# Changing this file is a reviewable diff in this repository's own history: a format
# change arrives as a pull request, never as a silent upstream shift under a build.
#
# `conformance/sync.sh` reads this file. `conformance/sync.sh --verify` re-checks the
# vendored copy under tests/Affiant.Conformance.Tests/protocol/ against SHA256SUMS,
# which is what CI runs, so a local edit to a vendored fixture cannot pass unnoticed.

